1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:02,383
Slicing and list operations.

2
00:00:02,383 --> 00:00:03,249
Four moves you'll

3
00:00:03,249 --> 00:00:04,532
use every day.

4
00:00:04,532 --> 00:00:06,279
Same list as last time.

5
00:00:06,279 --> 00:00:08,359
nums[1:4] takes a slice.

6
00:00:08,359 --> 00:00:09,963
It starts at index one, and

7
00:00:09,963 --> 00:00:11,960
stops before index four.

8
00:00:12,010 --> 00:00:13,074
The stop index is

9
00:00:13,074 --> 00:00:14,579
never included.

10
00:00:14,629 --> 00:00:16,002
nums[::2] takes

11
00:00:16,002 --> 00:00:18,258
every second item.

12
00:00:18,508 --> 00:00:21,966
And nums[::-1] reverses it.

13
00:00:22,316 --> 00:00:23,988
Every slice is a new list.

14
00:00:23,988 --> 00:00:26,184
The original never changes.

15
00:00:26,234 --> 00:00:27,056
append adds an

16
00:00:27,056 --> 00:00:28,603
item to the end.

17
00:00:28,753 --> 00:00:30,118
insert(0, 5) puts a

18
00:00:30,118 --> 00:00:31,703
value at the front,

19
00:00:31,703 --> 00:00:32,705
so every other item

20
00:00:32,705 --> 00:00:34,307
has to shift right.

21
00:00:34,457 --> 00:00:35,692
pop removes the last

22
00:00:35,692 --> 00:00:37,580
item, and returns it.

23
00:00:37,830 --> 00:00:38,656
Recap.

24
00:00:38,656 --> 00:00:39,821
Slices are copies,

25
00:00:39,821 --> 00:00:41,405
and stop is excluded.

26
00:00:41,405 --> 00:00:42,625
append is fast.

27
00:00:42,625 --> 00:00:43,872
Inserting at the front

28
00:00:43,872 --> 00:00:45,694
is slow on big lists.

29
00:00:46,044 --> 00:00:47,019
Next up: lists

30
00:00:47,019 --> 00:00:48,185
versus arrays.

31
00:00:48,185 --> 00:00:50,122
Follow for the whole series.
